 "capsule": "Operating under Iraq's 2005 federal, parliamentary constitution, the Republic of Iraq faced an existential crisis in June 2014 when Islamic State (ISIS) forces seized Mosul and much of the north and west; Prime Minister Haider al-Abadi's government, backed by the Popular Mobilization Forces and a U.S.-led coalition, declared victory over ISIS by December 2017. Subsequent governments under Adil Abdul-Mahdi, Mustafa al-Kadhimi, and Mohammed Shia' al-Sudani governed through mass protests and economic crisis while preserving the constitution's federal parliamentary republic structure into 2025.",
